From d51f74849354c204ca7aa024a5a88fb62baabd2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter M <petermm@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:40:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] rtems-esp-wifi: manage shared PHY and per-target clock
 lifecycles

Consolidated from the following downstream patches. Original rationale
and provenance are retained below; source licensing is unchanged.

Keep the common first-enable/calibration/tracking state machine together
with its C3/C5/C6/S31 clock and critical-section implementations.

Original-patch: 0009-esp32c5-follow-idf-phy-lifecycle.patch
Original-author: Peter M <petermm@gmail.com>
Original-date: 2026-10-19T21:40:15+02:00
AtomVM-origin-commit: d3ae147cdd0922d3ac24125271a9f4d485712115

rtems-esp-wifi: follow ESP-IDF C5 PHY and clock lifecycle

Use ESP-IDF LL clock operations rather than enabling all register bits.
Calibrate on first PHY enable, wake on subsequent enables, track the PLL
while active and close RF/temperature sensing on disable. Match the C5
baseband watchdog settings and retain initialized Wi-Fi clocks.

Original-patch: 0010-esp32c3-follow-idf-phy-lifecycle.patch
Original-author: Peter M <petermm@gmail.com>
Original-date: 2026-10-19T22:05:10+02:00
AtomVM-origin-commit: b8857620c4d615469e5d3d26f852e6b64172d4d8

rtems-esp-wifi: align C3 startup and PHY lifecycle with IDF

Use IDF's C3 modem and low-power clock initialization and targeted analog
bus setup. Share first-enable calibration, wake/disable and PLL tracking
with C5, including temporary calibration storage. Select C3 combo PHY mode
and save/restore its digital registers across disable/wakeup. Preserve nested
C3 PHY/Wi-Fi/I2C interrupt levels and place these critical hooks in IRAM.

Original-patch: 0011-esp32c6-follow-idf-phy-lifecycle.patch
Original-author: Peter M. <petermm@gmail.com>
Original-date: 2026-10-19T22:16:49+02:00
AtomVM-origin-commit: 6cb93d642fc96c0c816e1f70f5482666fb1063df

Align ESP32-C6 modem clocks and PHY lifecycle with ESP-IDF

Use C6 LL clock dependencies, combined-radio calibration on first enable,
PLL tracking and RF shutdown. Preserve nested Wi-Fi/PHY/I2C interrupt state
in IRAM. C6 uses the non-retention wakeup path; backup DMA is C3-specific.

Original-patch: 0012-esp32s31-follow-idf-phy-lifecycle.patch
Original-author: Peter M. <petermm@gmail.com>
Original-date: 2026-10-19T22:26:47+02:00
AtomVM-origin-commit: eacba5ef91f83c7150d582bff3a2ec6a734f3b80

Align ESP32-S31 modem clocks, PHY lifecycle and SMP critical sections

Use specific ESP-IDF clock dependencies and first-enable PHY calibration.
Preserve per-hart PMA mappings, apply the S31 peripheral access workaround,
and provide recursive SMP-safe Wi-Fi/PHY/I2C critical sections in IRAM.
